  faqs: [
    { question: "How do I find IB and IGCSE tutors in Cuttack?", answer: "Tell IB Gram your child's IB programme, subject, level and exam session, and we shortlist tutors who have actually taught that exact course. Cuttack has no IB school of its own, so location plays no part in the shortlist; syllabus fit does. Once we confirm a slot that suits your evening, you sit a free trial online before committing to anything, and a different tutor gets suggested if the first one is not right." },
    { question: "Do you offer IGCSE home tutors in Cuttack for Cambridge and Edexcel?", answer: "Yes, matched for both boards, delivered as online home tuition rather than a visit to your door. A Cambridge student is matched on syllabus code and tier, Mathematics 0580 Extended or Chemistry 0620 for instance, and an Edexcel student on specification and Foundation or Higher tier, each taught from that board's own past papers and mark scheme rather than a generic one." },
    { question: "Do your tutors visit homes in Cuttack?", answer: "Tutors do not come to a Cuttack home for a lesson; that arrangement exists only in Gurugram and a few pockets of Delhi NCR, nowhere else in the country. What happens instead in Cuttack is live one-to-one tuition over video, with a shared digital whiteboard doing the work a physical visit otherwise would. It is genuinely private tuition delivered to your home, just not by someone walking through the door." },
    { question: "Does any school in Cuttack itself offer IB or IGCSE?", answer: "No school inside Cuttack's city limits currently teaches the IB or a Cambridge or Pearson Edexcel IGCSE syllabus; the city's schools run CBSE, ICSE or the Odisha State Board. Families who want either programme generally enrol their child at SAI International School or KIIT International School, both around half an hour away in Bhubaneswar, or arrange a boarding placement further afield." },
    { question: "Which Bhubaneswar schools do Cuttack IB and IGCSE families actually use?", answer: "SAI International School in Chandrasekharpur combines CBSE with Cambridge IGCSE and the IB Career-related Programme, while KIIT International School in Patia runs Cambridge Lower Secondary and IGCSE up to Grade 10 before moving students into the IB Diploma Programme for the last two years. Both sit roughly a half-hour drive from central Cuttack." },
    { question: "What does an IB or IGCSE tutor in Cuttack cost?", answer: "It depends on the programme and level, the subject, how long a session runs and how recently the tutor taught it, and your exact rate gets confirmed before the trial rather than afterwards. Diploma subjects at Higher Level typically cost more than MYP or IGCSE Core work. Every lesson being online removes any travel charge, and since nothing is locked into a long contract, you can pause or stop whenever it suits you." },
    { question: "Is there a free trial class before I commit?", answer: "Every match opens with one. Your child works through a real topic from their actual syllabus with the tutor online, at no cost and no obligation either way. A short first-month plan follows the trial, and from there you decide whether to go ahead, ask for a change, or try someone else entirely." },
    { question: "Can a tutor help with IB Internal Assessments for a Cuttack student?", answer: "Tutors guide an IA without ever writing part of it themselves. That guidance covers choosing a workable research question, unpacking what an assessment criterion is actually looking for, planning how data gets collected, and giving honest feedback on drafts. Anything that crosses into writing or rewriting the assessed work itself breaches IB integrity rules, so it is a request IB Gram tutors turn down every time." },
    { question: "Which IB Diploma subjects can you help with for a Cuttack student?", answer: "Coverage spans the major DP subject groups a small Cuttack cohort actually needs: both Maths strands at HL and SL, Physics, Chemistry, Biology, Economics, Business Management and English A most often, alongside Theory of Knowledge and Extended Essay support." },
    { question: "Do you tutor IB MYP and PYP students from Cuttack, not only the Diploma?", answer: "The whole IB continuum is covered, not just the Diploma. MYP work concentrates on criterion-based analysis in the sciences and language subjects, plus steady progress on the Personal Project's process journal. PYP sessions build reading, writing and number confidence, along with the research skills the Exhibition eventually needs, usually in short, regular slots around a Bhubaneswar school commute." },
    { question: "Is online tutoring as effective as in-person tuition for a Cuttack student?", answer: "It works well, arguably better here than the alternative, since Cuttack has no local specialist at all for a Higher Level IB subject or a specific IGCSE code. A shared whiteboard, screen-shared past papers and recorded worked examples replace almost everything a tutor sitting beside your child would otherwise offer, while opening the choice of tutor to genuine specialists based anywhere in India." },
    { question: "How are IB Gram tutors verified for Cuttack students?", answer: "Every tutor is checked on qualifications, how recently they have taught the exact subject and level in question, and how they approach assessment criteria, before ever being introduced to a family. Because Cuttack has no local school to draw a tutor pool from, the bar is someone who has genuinely taught that syllabus recently, not a confident generalist. The free trial then lets you judge that for yourself." },
    { question: "When should my child in Cuttack start IB or IGCSE tutoring?", answer: "Ideally at the start of the course, Class 11 for the Diploma, Grade 9 for IGCSE, which leaves time to fix foundations well before internal exams, IA deadlines and predicted grades arrive. Starting later, even in the final year, can still move the needle, provided tutoring stays focused on the highest-value topics and past papers rather than trying to cover everything." },
    { question: "My child is switching from CBSE or the State Board to IB or IGCSE. Can a tutor based in Cuttack help?", answer: "This is one of the more common starting points here, since no school in the city runs IB or IGCSE from day one. Content is rarely the real gap; exam style is. Command words such as 'explain', 'evaluate' and 'justify' need direct teaching, along with new habits around IA or coursework planning, and starting the summer before the actual switch gives that time to settle." },
    { question: "Can sessions happen on weekends or after school hours for a Cuttack family?", answer: "Weekday evenings once school and any coaching class wrap up, plus weekend mornings, are what most Cuttack families book. Scheduling works around the city's pre-monsoon heat, when an earlier evening slot is often preferred, and around Durga Puja and Bali Jatra. Adding a second weekly slot before mocks or an exam sitting is simple to arrange online." },
    { question: "What happens if we are not happy with the tutor in Cuttack?", answer: "Say so, and another tutor gets found. Progress is reviewed with families every few weeks specifically so a mismatch does not drag on, and there is no expectation that a child persists with someone who is not working out. Nothing here runs on a long contract, so pausing or stopping altogether carries no penalty either." },
    { question: "Is IB Gram affiliated with any Cuttack or Bhubaneswar school, or with the IB or Cambridge?", answer: "No. IB Gram operates independently and has no affiliation, endorsement or representation arrangement with any school, the International Baccalaureate Organization, Cambridge Assessment International Education or Pearson Edexcel. Schools named on this page simply describe where Cuttack families actually study, and tutors work to that school's calendar and the relevant board's own published syllabus." },
  ],

